{"hierarchy":{"reference":"doc:\/\/Statoscope\/tutorials\/StatoscopeTutorial","paths":[]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Statoscope\/tutorials\/StatoscopeTutorial","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[{"title":"Statoscope basics","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Statoscope is a small library to build apps with state management,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"testing, effects management and dependency injection.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It ships two patterns for a scope’s state, covered in the two chapters"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"below: "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reducer"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Reducer"},{"type":"text","text":"-annotated struct with a static"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"update()"},{"type":"text","text":" over a single state struct — is recommended for new"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"features. "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Statoscope (Classic)"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — a class with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Published"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"properties — is the easy migration path for bringing an existing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ViewModel-shaped screen into Statoscope."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"hero","action":{"overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"text":"Get started","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Statoscope\/tutorials\/Statoscope\/01-01-StateAndWhen-Reducer","overridingTitle":"Get started","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}},{"kind":"volume","content":[],"image":null,"chapters":[{"tutorials":["doc:\/\/Statoscope\/tutorials\/Statoscope\/01-01-StateAndWhen-Reducer","doc:\/\/Statoscope\/tutorials\/Statoscope\/01-02-StateWhenAndEffects-Reducer","doc:\/\/Statoscope\/tutorials\/Statoscope\/01-03-Middleware-Reducer","doc:\/\/Statoscope\/tutorials\/Statoscope\/01-04-Injection-Reducer","doc:\/\/Statoscope\/tutorials\/Statoscope\/01-05-Scopes-Reducer","doc:\/\/Statoscope\/tutorials\/Statoscope\/01-06-Testing-Reducer"],"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The recommended way to build new Statoscope features: a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Reducer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"struct, a single "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State"},{"type":"text","text":", a static "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"update()"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@SubState"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@SuperState"},{"type":"text","text":" for composing scopes — no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"self"},{"type":"text","text":", no scattered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Published"},{"type":"text","text":" properties, no reentrancy hole to worry about."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Reducers (Recommended)"},{"tutorials":["doc:\/\/Statoscope\/tutorials\/Statoscope\/01-01-StateAndWhen","doc:\/\/Statoscope\/tutorials\/Statoscope\/01-02-StateWhenAndEffects","doc:\/\/Statoscope\/tutorials\/Statoscope\/01-03-Middleware","doc:\/\/Statoscope\/tutorials\/Statoscope\/01-04-Injection","doc:\/\/Statoscope\/tutorials\/Statoscope\/01-05-Scopes","doc:\/\/Statoscope\/tutorials\/Statoscope\/01-06-Testing"],"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The original, class-based pattern — "},{"code":"Statostore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"code":"@Published","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"properties and an instance "},{"code":"update()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Start here if you’re migrating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an existing "},{"code":"ObservableObject","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/ViewModel-shaped screen: its shape maps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"closely onto what you already have."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Statoscope (Classic)"}],"name":null}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/tutorials\/statoscopetutorial"]}],"metadata":{"categoryPathComponent":"StatoscopeTutorial","category":"Statoscope Architecture","estimatedTime":"5hr 5min","role":"overview","title":"Statoscope basics"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"kind":"overview","references":{"doc://Statoscope/tutorials/StatoscopeTutorial":{"url":"\/tutorials\/statoscopetutorial","role":"overview","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Statoscope is a small library to build apps with state management,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"testing, effects management and dependency injection.","type":"text"}],"title":"Statoscope basics","kind":"overview","identifier":"doc:\/\/Statoscope\/tutorials\/StatoscopeTutorial"},"doc://Statoscope/tutorials/Statoscope/01-05-Scopes":{"kind":"project","url":"\/tutorials\/statoscope\/01-05-scopes","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Statoscope\/tutorials\/Statoscope\/01-05-Scopes","title":"Scopes","role":"project","estimatedTime":"30min","abstract":[{"text":"In complex applications, managing all state and events in a single Statostore quickly becomes unsustainable. To scale effectively, we need to split the app’s state and events into separate parts or Scopes. This process can sometimes be straightforward, but other times, developers may feel compelled to separate state and events that are closely tied together due to business logic. In this tutorial, we’ll focus on how to organize app state into different scopes to maintain scalability.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Statoscope/tutorials/Statoscope/01-02-StateWhenAndEffects-Reducer":{"url":"\/tutorials\/statoscope\/01-02-statewhenandeffects-reducer","role":"project","type":"topic","estimatedTime":"20min","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The Reducer counterpart of "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Statoscope\/tutorials\/Statoscope\/01-02-StateWhenAndEffects","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":": trigger effects that report"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"back to your reducer as a new "},{"code":"When","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" event, with the same synchronous update contract,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"now expressed as a pure static function.","type":"text"}],"title":"State, When and Effects (Reducer)","kind":"project","identifier":"doc:\/\/Statoscope\/tutorials\/Statoscope\/01-02-StateWhenAndEffects-Reducer"},"doc://Statoscope/tutorials/Statoscope/01-01-StateAndWhen":{"url":"\/tutorials\/statoscope\/01-01-stateandwhen","role":"project","type":"topic","estimatedTime":"20min","abstract":[{"text":"Define a scope object with state member variables representing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a part of your app’s status, define the events that may affect","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this state, and create a view to display the state.","type":"text"}],"title":"Create a simple Scope","identifier":"doc:\/\/Statoscope\/tutorials\/Statoscope\/01-01-StateAndWhen","kind":"project"},"doc://Statoscope/tutorials/Statoscope/01-03-Middleware":{"estimatedTime":"30min","url":"\/tutorials\/statoscope\/01-03-middleware","kind":"project","role":"project","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Understand how the single entry point enables pretty interesting features"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Statoscope\/tutorials\/Statoscope\/01-03-Middleware","title":"Single entry point and\/or middlewares"},"doc://Statoscope/tutorials/Statoscope/01-04-Injection":{"estimatedTime":"30min","url":"\/tutorials\/statoscope\/01-04-injection","kind":"project","role":"project","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn how to easily design dependencies and inject them into your scopes. Dependency injection simplifies the structure of your code by externalizing the management of dependencies, making your code more modular, testable, and flexible. In this tutorial, we will demonstrate dependency injection using an example of a simple news feed application."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Statoscope\/tutorials\/Statoscope\/01-04-Injection","title":"Dependency Injection"},"doc://Statoscope/tutorials/Statoscope/01-04-Injection-Reducer":{"url":"\/tutorials\/statoscope\/01-04-injection-reducer","kind":"project","identifier":"doc:\/\/Statoscope\/tutorials\/Statoscope\/01-04-Injection-Reducer","role":"project","estimatedTime":"25min","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"This is the Reducer-pattern counterpart to "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Statoscope\/tutorials\/Statoscope\/01-04-Injection","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":": same goal — externalize system dependencies (dates, persistence, network) so business logic stays testable — expressed with "},{"code":"Injectable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"ReducerDependencies","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"dependencies.resolve()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" inside a static "},{"code":"update()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instead of "},{"code":"@Injected","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" properties on a class."}],"title":"Dependency Injection (Reducer)","type":"topic"},"doc://Statoscope/tutorials/Statoscope/01-05-Scopes-Reducer":{"role":"project","estimatedTime":"30min","identifier":"doc:\/\/Statoscope\/tutorials\/Statoscope\/01-05-Scopes-Reducer","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Reducer counterpart of the classic Scopes tutorial. Splitting one growing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"struct into a tree of ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Reducer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" scopes, connected with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@SubState"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@SuperState"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"keeps each scope’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"When"},{"type":"text","text":" focused on one concern instead of one struct"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"absorbing everything the screen needs to do.","type":"text"}],"title":"Scopes (Reducer)","url":"\/tutorials\/statoscope\/01-05-scopes-reducer","kind":"project","type":"topic"},"doc://Statoscope/tutorials/Statoscope/01-01-StateAndWhen-Reducer":{"kind":"project","url":"\/tutorials\/statoscope\/01-01-stateandwhen-reducer","type":"topic","title":"Create a simple Reducer","identifier":"doc:\/\/Statoscope\/tutorials\/Statoscope\/01-01-StateAndWhen-Reducer","role":"project","estimatedTime":"15min","abstract":[{"text":"Define a ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Reducer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with a single ","type":"text"},{"code":"State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" struct and a static ","type":"text"},{"code":"update","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" function, then build a SwiftUI view and tests on top of it. This is the Reducer-pattern counterpart to the classic State-and-When tutorial, and the recommended way to start a new Statoscope feature.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Statoscope/tutorials/Statoscope/01-06-Testing":{"kind":"project","title":"Scopes","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Statoscope\/tutorials\/Statoscope\/01-06-Testing","url":"\/tutorials\/statoscope\/01-06-testing","role":"project","estimatedTime":"30min","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"In complex applications, managing all state and events in a single Statostore quickly becomes unsustainable. To scale effectively, we need to split the app’s state and events into separate parts or Scopes. This process can sometimes be straightforward, but other times, developers may feel compelled to separate state and events that are closely tied together due to business logic. In this tutorial, we’ll focus on how to organize app state into different scopes to maintain scalability."}]},"doc://Statoscope/tutorials/Statoscope/01-02-StateWhenAndEffects":{"url":"\/tutorials\/statoscope\/01-02-statewhenandeffects","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Statoscope\/tutorials\/Statoscope\/01-02-StateWhenAndEffects","role":"project","estimatedTime":"30min","abstract":[{"text":"Trigger effects that will get back to your scope as a new When event.","type":"text"}],"title":"State, When and Effects","kind":"project"},"doc://Statoscope/tutorials/Statoscope/01-03-Middleware-Reducer":{"role":"project","type":"topic","url":"\/tutorials\/statoscope\/01-03-middleware-reducer","identifier":"doc:\/\/Statoscope\/tutorials\/Statoscope\/01-03-Middleware-Reducer","abstract":[{"code":"Store<R>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — the class the ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Reducer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" macro generates for you — is built on the same","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"single-entry-point foundation as classic Statostore, so ","type":"text"},{"code":"addMiddleWare","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" works exactly the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same way here. Nothing to relearn: you get event interception, logging, and crash"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reporting for free."}],"kind":"project","estimatedTime":"20min","title":"Single entry point and\/or middlewares (Reducer)"},"doc://Statoscope/tutorials/Statoscope/01-06-Testing-Reducer":{"kind":"project","url":"\/tutorials\/statoscope\/01-06-testing-reducer","title":"Testing Reducers","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Statoscope\/tutorials\/Statoscope\/01-06-Testing-Reducer","role":"project","estimatedTime":"25min","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"This is the Reducer-pattern counterpart to the classic Testing tutorial. We’ll build a small"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"news feed feature — a parent "},{"code":"NewsFeedReducer","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with a child "},{"code":"NewsFeedArticleReducer","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — and write"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the full range of acceptance tests against it: basic flow, effects, child-store navigation, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dependency injection. Every state assertion in this tutorial reads through "},{"code":".state.","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", since a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Reducer’s data always lives one level down from the "},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" itself."}]}}}